From 94b2c1897748611ac5c2f828eed07bc9e910eefa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:57:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: balance sessions across replicated Rockchip M2M cores

RGA3, VEPU121 and RKVDEC currently reject all but the first instance of
each compatible. Keep a single V4L2 frontend and enroll the remaining
instances as independently scheduled hardware backends instead.

Pick the ready core with the fewest open sessions before allocating
command or video buffers. Keep that assignment until close so that
buffer DMA mappings, decoder references, registers, IRQs, watchdogs and
runtime PM always belong to the same physical device. Each core uses
its own existing M2M queue; concurrent sessions can execute in parallel.
Keep frontend/queue ioctl locking consistent across those sessions.
This is session-level parallelism, not splitting one frame across cores.

Secondary cores defer until their frontend is ready and take managed
device links to order teardown. Probe failures do not enroll partially
initialized cores, and failed opens return their session reservations.
Only the leader registers video/media nodes; request-backed buffers on
workers continue to use the frontend media device.

Expose documented per-core session, submitted, completed and error
counters for validation alongside IRQ deltas and checked output buffers.
Also unwind Hantro clock/runtime-PM references when a job fails to start.

Validation: affected drivers cross-build; host execution of the actual
pool helper with mocked OF/sysfs/device operations, including 8000
concurrent acquire/release operations and registration failure rollback.
Hardware multi-core validation is pending the user's board run.

Signed-off-by: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
