diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-v4l2-m2m-corepool b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-v4l2-m2m-corepool
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..72ba7cab0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-v4l2-m2m-corepool
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../m2m_core_users
+Date:           November 2026
+Contact:        RK3588 board maintainers
+Description:
+                Number of open V4L2 sessions assigned to this physical core.
+                A family exposes one frontend. Sessions are balanced across
+                ready cores before allocating DMA buffers and keep core
+                affinity until close. The value includes idle open sessions.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../m2m_core_submitted
+Date:           November 2026
+Contact:        RK3588 board maintainers
+Description:
+                Read-only count of jobs dispatched to this physical core
+                since probe. Includes jobs that subsequently fail to start.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../m2m_core_completed
+Date:           November 2026
+Contact:        RK3588 board maintainers
+Description:
+                Read-only count of successfully completed jobs on this core
+                since probe. Aggregate together with IRQ and output evidence
+                when validating concurrent use of multiple hardware cores.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../m2m_core_errors
+Date:           November 2026
+Contact:        RK3588 board maintainers
+Description:
+                Read-only count of jobs completed with an error, including
+                existing decoder watchdog recovery, since probe. These
+                counters do not expose a new userspace core-selection API.
